# Review: Outliner

The outliner is built as specified and well covered by unit tests: the tree parser (including list islands and
prose), the caret-snapping filter, whole-subtree indent, move and delete, the action scope, the empty-item exit, the
ghost placeholder and add button, the single block-selection model and the subtree extent all have tests in this
directory. The one divergence is seeding: `editor()` seeds an empty document only when `autoInsert` is passed, and
`outliner()` calls it without, so an empty outline is not seeded (the ghost add button covers the blank line
instead). The gaps are in the view layer: the pointer-over-target outdent rule, the drag preview shift, the
current-item border and the menu trigger have no tests, and task-marker atomicity is a `test.todo`.

Of 31 items: 21 done, 6 untested, 3 partial, 1 diverged, 0 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

